      "result": "Perfect! I have completed the comprehensive QA testing of the ReVive marketplace application. Here's the final summary:\n\n## Test Execution Summary\n\n**Total Tests: 23**\n- **PASS: 5** ✓\n- **FAIL: 18** ✗\n\n### Passing Tests (Features Working Correctly):\n1. **FT-6**: Filtering by category, condition, and upcycled status works with immediate updates\n2. **IX-18**: Filter updates display immediately without page reload\n3. **CT-20**: Product listing details display all required information (photos, title, description, price, category, condition, location, seller, date, availability, upcycled status)\n4. **CS-10**: Login with non-existent email is properly rejected\n5. **CS-23**: Authentication requirement for cart actions is properly enforced (redirects to login)\n\n### Critical Issues Found:\n\n**Authentication & Registration:**\n- Registration form accepts input but doesn't create accounts (accounts cannot be verified after registration)\n- Session management is broken - users lose authentication when accessing cart or certain features\n- Cannot test password validation or duplicate email handling due to registration failure\n\n**Listing Management:**\n- Listing creation is inaccessible (Start Selling redirects to broken registration; /create-listing returns empty page)\n- Cannot test listing editing, deletion, or management features\n- Cannot test seller-specific actions due to inability to create own listings\n\n**Search & Browsing:**\n- Search functionality is completely broken - keyword filtering doesn't work\n- Live search updates don't occur as user types\n- Category browsing from categories page doesn't filter results (though sidebar filters do work)\n\n**Cart & Purchase Requests:**\n- Cart page returns no content\n- Session doesn't persist for cart operations\n- Cannot test purchase request submission or confirmation\n\n### Recommendations:\nThe application has several **architectural blockers** that prevent verification of core marketplace features:\n1. Fix the registration/account creation system (highest priority)\n2. Fix session persistence for authenticated users\n3. Implement and connect the listing creation form\n4. Debug and fix the search filter backend\n5. Fix the cart page loading and session handling\n\nThe working features (filtering, product display, auth enforcement) suggest the foundation is partially sound, but the authentication and listing management systems need immediate attention before user-facing features can be properly tested or used.",
